# Never use em dashes

Do NOT use em dashes (—) or the `&mdash;` entity ANYWHERE: chat replies,
code, comments, commit messages, UI copy, or docs. This is a hard rule with
no exceptions.

Instead, do one of:

- Split into two sentences with a period. (preferred)
- Use a spaced hyphen `" - "` when a short connector is needed.
- Use a colon or parentheses where they fit.

Also avoid en dashes (–) in prose. Use a hyphen, or write "to" for numeric
ranges (e.g. "1 to 12", not "1–12").

<example>
BAD:  Voting has closed — results below.
GOOD: Voting has closed. Results below.
GOOD: Voting has closed - results below.
</example>
